course: dictionary
lesson: 9697
title: Suggestions: ideas and hints
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A suggestion is an idea or plan that you offer for others to think about. «Let's play outside» is a suggestion: you are inviting your friends to choose it, and they can say yes or no.
explain: A suggestion can also be a small sign or hint of something. «There was a suggestion of a smile on her face» means she was almost smiling, only a little. Nobody said she was smiling; you can just see a hint of it.
explain: Read the words around suggestion to tell which meaning it has. If people are planning something together, it is probably an idea. If the words describe a face, a sound or a feeling, it is probably a hint. Then try your meaning in the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: Suggestion is a noun, and its plural is suggestions. It comes from the verb suggest. In class, teachers ask «Any suggestions?» when they want pupils to share ideas for making work better.
fact: A suggestion is an idea or plan that you offer for others to think about.
fact: A suggestion can also be a small sign or hint of something, like a suggestion of a smile.
fact: «Make a suggestion» means to offer an idea.
fact: «At someone's suggestion» means because someone suggested it.
fact: A spellcheck can suggest the wrong word, so always read its suggestion before you accept it.
exercise: In «Let's play outside», what kind of suggestion is it? | A small hint of a smile | *An idea or plan for others to think about | A list of spelling words | A loud shout across the playground
exercise: «There was a suggestion of a smile on her face.» What does suggestion mean here? | A spelling test | A plan for a party | *A small sign or hint | A loud shout
exercise: Ms Hale says, «Any suggestions?» What is she asking for? | A test on spelling | Stories about dragons | Money for a school trip | *Ideas to make the work better
test: Mum says, «Shall we go to the park?» What is her suggestion? | A spelling word | *A plan to go to the park | A hint of rain on the window | A loud shout
test: A phone says, «It may suggest the wrong word, so read the suggestion.» What should you do? | *Read it and check it makes sense | Ignore all spelling | Accept it without reading | Throw the phone away
exam: Which sentence uses suggestion to mean a small hint? | «The box is full of books.» | «Let's go swimming tomorrow.» | *«She gave the tiniest suggestion of a smile.» | «My dog is called Biscuit.»
